50 712 Td () Tj
50 694 Td (Cells are the basic units of life. All living organisms are composed of cells, and new cells) Tj
50 676 Td (arise from existing cells. The cell theory states these three principles.) Tj
50 658 Td () Tj
50 640 Td (Prokaryotic cells, such as bacteria, lack a nucleus and membrane-bound organelles. Their) Tj
50 622 Td (genetic material is a single circular chromosome located in a region called the nucleoid. They) Tj
50 604 Td (are typically smaller and simpler than eukaryotic cells.) Tj
50 586 Td () Tj
50 568 Td (Eukaryotic cells possess a true nucleus surrounded by a nuclear membrane and contain) Tj
50 550 Td (membrane-bound organelles such as mitochondria, the endoplasmic reticulum, the Golgi) Tj
50 532 Td (apparatus, and chloroplasts in plant cells.) Tj
50 514 Td () Tj
