50 712 Td () Tj
50 694 Td (The cell cycle is the series of events that a cell goes through as it grows and divides. It) Tj
50 676 Td (consists of interphase and the mitotic phase.) Tj
50 658 Td () Tj
50 640 Td (Interphase is the longest phase and includes G1, S, and G2 stages. In G1 the cell grows and) Tj
50 622 Td (carries out normal functions. During S phase, DNA is replicated, so each chromosome now) Tj
50 604 Td (consists of two sister chromatids joined at the centromere. In G2 the cell prepares for) Tj
50 586 Td (division.) Tj
50 568 Td () Tj
50 550 Td (Mitosis has four stages: prophase, metaphase, anaphase, and telophase. In prophase,) Tj
50 532 Td (chromosomes condense and the mitotic spindle forms. In metaphase, chromosomes align at the) Tj
50 514 Td (metaphase plate. In anaphase, sister chromatids separate and move to opposite poles. In) Tj
50 496 Td (telophase, two new nuclei form.) Tj
50 478 Td () Tj
50 460 Td (Cytokinesis divides the cytoplasm, and in animal cells a cleavage furrow pinches the cell in) Tj
50 442 Td (two. The result is two genetically identical daughter cells.) Tj
