50 658 Td () Tj
50 640 Td (Glycolysis occurs in the cytoplasm and splits glucose into two molecules of pyruvate,) Tj
50 622 Td (producing a net of two ATP and two NADH. It does not require oxygen.) Tj
50 604 Td () Tj
50 586 Td (The citric acid cycle, also called the Krebs cycle, occurs in the mitochondrial matrix.) Tj
50 568 Td (Acetyl-CoA enters the cycle, and each turn produces NADH, FADH2, and ATP while releasing) Tj
50 550 Td (carbon dioxide.) Tj
50 532 Td () Tj
50 514 Td (Oxidative phosphorylation occurs along the inner mitochondrial membrane. The electron) Tj
50 496 Td (transport chain passes electrons from NADH and FADH2 to oxygen, pumping protons across the) Tj
